<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2019-boundary-22--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2019-boundary-22: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.10";
    dc:description "The closing summary states how agents scaled up, by adding memory, anticipation, and networks to homeostatic loops under surprise minimization. Extant physiology can be described in those terms in more than one order. No dataset records the succession. The claim is a historical schema without a distinguishing test.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Homeostasis, memory, and prediction can be ascribed to living systems after the fact. A required evolutionary sequence from loops, through delays, to networks is not a variable in phylogenetic or experimental datasets.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Alternative orders of the same ingredients fit the same modern organisms.", "The scaling path is a narrative of how agency must have been built.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.76"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.098"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2019-boundary-22--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
